#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 1140.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199257} :activity/id #uuid "be4ab3e9-bce0-5963-aee7-f144ec42c0bc" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049110 :topic/id #uuid "db34e5aa-cabd-518f-9dff-177947a5ce3a" :topic/math-academy-id 4166} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199256 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199454 :tutorial/content "Recall that a lamina's *center of mass* is the point $(\\overline{x}, \\overline{y})$ where its total mass could be concentrated to give the same total moment about the coordinate axes as the original lamina. \n\nThe center of mass of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda(x,y)$ is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overline{x},\\overline{y}) = \\left( \\dfrac{M_y}{m}, \\dfrac{M_x}{m} \\right),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $\\displaystyle m = \\iint \\limits_D \\lambda (x,y) \\: \\textrm{d}A$ is the mass of the lamina,\n\n- $\\displaystyle M_x = \\iint\\limits_D y \\, \\lambda (x,y) \\: \\textrm{d}A\\:$ is the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- $\\displaystyle M_y = \\iint\\limits_D x \\, \\lambda (x,y) \\: \\textrm{d}A$ is the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis.\n\nRemember that if we could place a fulcrum under our lamina at its center of mass, it would balance perfectly." :tutorial/id #uuid "dbc92201-9cb2-54d6-9ac9-8ee49bf8c4e5" :tutorial/math-academy-id 4905 :tutorial/title "Center of Mass"} :step/id #uuid "274308ee-bab4-54df-9e77-953f260e7982" :step/math-academy-id 30624 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199258}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199257 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199455 :tutorial/content "In this lesson, we'll learn how to determine the center of mass of a thin lamina whose mass is unevenly distributed. \n\nWe describe the mass distribution across a lamina using its mass density function $\\lambda (x,y).$ This function tells us the *mass per unit area* at any point $(x,y)$ on the lamina.\n\nFor example, consider a thin plate with mass density function $\\lambda(x,y) = 6xy$ occupying the finite rectangular region $D$ between the lines $x=1,$ $x=2,$ $y=0,$ and $y=1.$ What is the moment of the plate about the $y$-axis?\n\nTo answer this, consider a point $(x,y) \\in D$ on the plate and a small rectangular piece with its bottom-left corner at $(x,y)$ and area $\\Delta{A},$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/8c/8cd947e542aaf7eb787abc7a846e87a2d03ccafa0987f3422928fdcba115da9e.png)\n\nIf $\\Delta{A}$ is very small, we can assume that our density function is approximately constant over the selected piece. As a result, the moment of this piece about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ{M}_{y} & ≈x\\cdot Δm \\\\  & ≈x\\cdot 6xy\\,ΔA \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}y\\,ΔA.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the total moment of the plate about the axis, we add together the moments of all such pieces and take the limit as $\\Delta{A} \\to 0.$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\nM_y =  \\iint\\limits_D 6x^2y \\: \\textrm{d}A.\n$$\n\n \n\nCarrying out the integration, we find that the moment of the plate about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}6{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}6{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{1}2y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =[{x}^{3}]_{x=1}^{x=2}\\cdot [{y}^{2}]_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =(8-1)\\cdot (1-0) \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe moment about the $x$-axis can be found similarly.\n\nIn general, the moments $M_x$ and $M_y$ of a lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda(x,y)$ about the $x$-axis and about the $y$-axis, respectively, are given by the following formulas:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\ {M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "7aa18cfe-acd7-5e17-982c-58eabc063404" :tutorial/math-academy-id 4906 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "751210ed-66b0-57b2-8130-be9ebe7e72a9" :step/math-academy-id 30625 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199330}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199258 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198364 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198238 :question/id #uuid "8199670b-efe4-537b-8f8a-228d567a0944" :question/math-academy-id "e-8182"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f7a06a8-0260-5b59-b3a5-c02ee03980d4" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198962} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198975} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235552} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281619} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281620} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281664} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281665} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281666} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419225} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419230} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419232} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419236} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419237}] :knowledge-point/title "Find the Center of Mass of a Plane Lamina"} :step/id #uuid "d8381e14-c44b-5f31-9e2d-03ef40423eb9" :step/math-academy-id 30626 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199259}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199259 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199456 :tutorial/content "When a lamina's mass density is constant, the center of mass depends only on the shape of the lamina. In cases like these, the center of mass is called the **centroid** of the lamina. The centroid of a shape corresponds to its geometrical center.\n\nSo, $\\lambda$ is constant, then the mass of the plate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda \\,dA \\\\  & =\\lambda {∬}_{D}\\,dA \\\\  & =\\lambda \\cdot {A}_{D},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $A_D$ denotes the area of $D.$ As a result, \n\n$$\nm = \\lambda \\cdot A_D \\qquad \\Longrightarrow \\qquad \\dfrac{\\lambda}{m} = \\dfrac{1}{A_D}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the formula for the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m} & =\\frac{1}{m}{∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda \\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{\\lambda }{m}{∬}_{D}x\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}x\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can similarly compute the $y$-coordinate.\n\nIn general, the centroid of a lamina $D$ with area $A_D$ is given by $(x_c, y_c),$ where\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle x_c = \\dfrac{1}{A_D} \\iint\\limits_D x \\, \\: \\textrm{d}A, \\qquad \n\\displaystyle y_c = \\dfrac{1}{A_D} \\iint\\limits_D y \\, \\: \\textrm{d}A.\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "aea964ff-901c-5b76-9fca-721d53f04354" :tutorial/math-academy-id 4907 :tutorial/title "Centroids"} :step/id #uuid "c6144c3d-16c1-5ac5-841d-01a96fe71c2e" :step/math-academy-id 30627 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199260}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199260 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198365 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198239 :question/id #uuid "37d7f2ae-90b0-5e6f-83c2-7cb21ed4f089" :question/math-academy-id "e-8183"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "255c9985-5d85-5fd5-a2b9-c4752f04afac" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198966} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198974} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281667} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281668} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281672} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281673} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419227} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419229} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419233} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419235} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419239} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508061}] :knowledge-point/title "Find the Centroid of a Plane Lamina"} :step/id #uuid "38ffe571-8650-5b48-a6db-d2d7374b7548" :step/math-academy-id 30628} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199329 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198406 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198048 :question/id #uuid "81b0b6e1-41c3-5329-806e-162b8b27b045" :question/math-academy-id "e-12466"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "804ee2d1-5590-534d-ae11-7d2c5614a9b1" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198654} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198973} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235551} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281586} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281587} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281613} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281615} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281616} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281680} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419228} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419231} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419238} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419240} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508048}] :knowledge-point/title "The Moment of a Plane Lamina About the Y-Axis"} :step/id #uuid "c6197786-2f72-519b-bd74-410c8f09a532" :step/math-academy-id 44879 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199256}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199330 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198407 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198049 :question/id #uuid "9294903c-1b4c-58b6-a878-7f2220ec763d" :question/math-academy-id "e-12470"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "444e9b54-f6d4-5b70-af49-d01556bb3135" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049267} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049333} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050326} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050409}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198629} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198652} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235550} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281559} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281560} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281562} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281582} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419224} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419226} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419234} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419241} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508098} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553507}] :knowledge-point/title "The Moment of a Plane Lamina About the X-Axis"} :step/id #uuid "6a2f3763-0f5f-5328-a240-5a9328c979b3" :step/math-academy-id 44905 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199329}}] :activity/title "Moments and Centers of Mass of Plane Laminas" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186198495}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046644} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508138} :activity/id #uuid "66c5f538-bf73-5738-ac9e-056fec289e7e" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049110 :topic/id #uuid "db34e5aa-cabd-518f-9dff-177947a5ce3a" :topic/math-academy-id 4166} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508117 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281587 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e521e4f-0860-5a65-9ac2-eda32bfca8ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279305} {:answer/id #uuid "4ff0cfbd-f9da-5245-a475-255ea08605cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279318} {:answer/id #uuid "8fdb2853-701b-5307-ad7e-d512948651d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279873} {:answer/id #uuid "ab21d0b4-eff6-548f-b2b3-7f4952880828" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280108} {:answer/id #uuid "fd58d3b2-06c6-5e92-89a3-b6bb6ae53691" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280809}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279305} :answer-field/id #uuid "c47ab8ca-3bde-5fba-a4a7-31651f3af0b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281176}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "fe9f4bda-1254-5b20-b5e7-335406a2dc03" :question/math-academy-id "q-163066" :question/problem "The lamina $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3y,\\,0\\le y\\le 1\\}$ has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=5xy.$ Find the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is represented as a type II plane region and $\\lambda (x,y)=5xy.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot 5xy\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}5{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3y}5{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}5y{\\int }_{0}^{3y}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}5y{[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=3y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}5y(9{y}^{3}-0)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}45{y}^{4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =[9{y}^{5}]_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "04149e10-de16-5e52-9d4c-e924df4e6c9a" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508168}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508138 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508098 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63becd05-2827-54e1-b25f-49475c7277d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507745} {:answer/id #uuid "a8e556e3-1b58-565c-8179-f27e71c39ec1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507835} {:answer/id #uuid "b7617195-3a4c-5cce-a014-90302c0f45d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507850} {:answer/id #uuid "ccd1812f-96df-5ea4-86f6-fc9ebbe2a707" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507881} {:answer/id #uuid "eae7226a-9ab7-55eb-9547-35faebb62155" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507917}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507917} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b8a70bd-cbd3-5bb7-9a20-2989c5769039" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507947}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c6e7ac3c-60bd-5c96-a837-e70ac483b403" :question/math-academy-id "q-162972" :question/problem "The lamina $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,-y\\le x\\le y\\}$ has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=6{x}^{2}.$ Find the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is represented as a type II plane region and $\\lambda (x,y)=6{x}^{2}.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\cdot 6{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}6{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-y}^{y}6{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2y[{\\int }_{-y}^{y}3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2y\\cdot {[{x}^{3}]}_{x=-y}^{x=y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2y\\cdot 2{y}^{3}\\text{ }\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4{y}^{4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{4}{5}{y}^{5}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "64412876-71ee-5320-bcb3-58c33e18f0b7" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508165}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508165 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281560 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "167e6409-5e3e-5efb-a712-07b360471d4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278790} {:answer/id #uuid "2732ae5b-753f-525a-b5e9-1120f08e3c31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278940} {:answer/id #uuid "775abca6-570c-5895-b34d-8941c17f178b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279658} {:answer/id #uuid "88d3bab5-4d08-59c8-a45a-f21f13e573d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279814} {:answer/id #uuid "f3d35eb7-48e3-5f6c-b3b0-c9bb57e1a8a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280726}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278940} :answer-field/id #uuid "e17aea6f-d602-5f51-a2f7-34b15c79c4b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281226}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9b4076e3-ab6e-5bdd-85c0-2781a4c652d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-162977" :question/problem "The lamina $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 3,\\,1\\le x\\le {e}^{y}\\}$ has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{1}{xy}.$ Find the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is represented as a type II plane region and $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{1}{xy}.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\cdot \\frac{1}{xy}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{y}}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡x]_{x=1}^{x={e}^{y}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=1}^{y=3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(9-1) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "e84e8b2b-1d47-5a7c-a608-fa747bd1a9cf" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508117}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508166 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508061 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e1b7da3-c426-532e-ac8e-720cc44224b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507632} {:answer/id #uuid "6511608d-c3ac-5e2b-8914-4eba27b60808" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507746} {:answer/id #uuid "6a9602ff-82fc-59fa-9526-6670ef4a4c21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507754} {:answer/id #uuid "71ace97c-298f-5384-84e5-5cec05c12f1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507764} {:answer/id #uuid "72c7b13e-659a-509a-a72a-ffc4f4cc555e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507765}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507632} :answer-field/id #uuid "77626c7e-6f8b-519e-9042-3f623f612a29" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507996}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "567a0e9f-c2af-5671-a94c-0c227edb1ded" :question/math-academy-id "q-163505" :question/problem "Consider the lamina that occupies the region $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt{{y}^{3}},\\,0\\le y\\le 1\\}.$ Given that the area of the lamina is $\\frac{2}{5}$ square units, find the $y$-coordinate of its centroid." :question/worked-solution "The centroid of a lamina $D$ with area ${A}_{D}$ is given by $({x}_{c},{y}_{c}),$ where\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}x\\,\\,\\text{d}A,\\,{y}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}y\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-coordinate of the centroid is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{c} & =\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{{y}^{3}}}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}y{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{{y}^{3}}}\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}y[x]_{x=0}^{x=\\sqrt{{y}^{3}}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\cdot \\sqrt{{y}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{5/2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{[\\frac{2{y}^{7/2}}{7}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "edd8ba29-7f85-5fb5-96c7-3b323408b5ac"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508168 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508048 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b78bae3-6dac-5231-bc72-0f224493d1ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507651} {:answer/id #uuid "461dd4bf-3120-534f-903c-0f6b43aa0379" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507706} {:answer/id #uuid "5f7de461-b87c-5895-81fe-a20fba2fc2fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507738} {:answer/id #uuid "9ee1ba58-3c47-5256-98f6-5f3213ad1570" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507821} {:answer/id #uuid "9f938d30-ac1a-58c2-b1e4-72cbfb1471d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507822}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507822} :answer-field/id #uuid "b671f817-f30d-58d1-9ad7-bc1f02d0b0c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508014}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1263ed3f-1cc0-53b6-a6ed-69fefa90cd2b" :question/math-academy-id "q-163164" :question/problem "A thin plate $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{15{y}^{2}}{x}$ is enclosed between the curve  $x=2-{y}^{2}$ and the line $x=1$ for $-1\\le y\\le 1.$ Find the moment of the plate about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is a type II plane region, as shown below.\n\n![](images/6c/6c78767d03e3429551498e651d982d99b6ceb72aa73422c5205bef296c9a1754.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2-{y}^{2},\\,-1\\le y\\le 1\\}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{15{y}^{2}}{x}.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot \\frac{15{y}^{2}}{x}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}15{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2-{y}^{2}}15{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}15{y}^{2}[{\\int }_{1}^{2-{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}15{y}^{2}[x]_{x=1}^{x=2-{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}15{y}^{2}(2-{y}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}15{y}^{2}-15{y}^{4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[5{y}^{3}-3{y}^{5}]}_{y=-1}^{y=1} \\\\  & =(5-3)-(-5+3) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "f8e51044-c774-57f1-9ffb-21331bca50b2" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508166}}] :activity/title "Moments and Centers of Mass of Plane Laminas" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507602}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046669} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553630} :activity/id #uuid "c995bd37-d5c7-5238-ad40-fa584e6d0cc9" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049110 :topic/id #uuid "db34e5aa-cabd-518f-9dff-177947a5ce3a" :topic/math-academy-id 4166} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553599 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281586 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "058f3f49-dd9b-5bcf-91d7-3a13b16a9e8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278643} {:answer/id #uuid "77ba5e2f-a104-5d77-9899-41ca53308fcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279660} {:answer/id #uuid "c21732aa-50b9-5374-b1cf-aafdcf9b532e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280296} {:answer/id #uuid "d3a28a67-2379-5f88-bd30-3f1a0be7c1a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280454} {:answer/id #uuid "f6bfa4ea-979d-50bf-aa25-25d0dbfd8906" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280752}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186280752} :answer-field/id #uuid "2417477b-102b-5b64-a662-c9071feb4de4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280895}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "950af147-dd8f-5a17-bc09-5c26666bfffb" :question/math-academy-id "q-163062" :question/problem "The lamina $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\le y\\le 0\\}$ has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=2{e}^{y}.$ Find the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is represented as a type I plane region and $\\lambda (x,y)=2{e}^{y}.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot 2{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2x{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}^{0}2x{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}2x[{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}^{0}{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}2x\\cdot [{e}^{y}]_{y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}^{y=0}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}2x(1-x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}2x-2{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{x}^{2}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{x=1/2}^{x=1} \\\\  & =(1-\\frac{2}{3})-(\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{12}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "1437a389-a86c-5d69-b2cf-23b43fd678dc" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553642}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553617 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281559 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03b80abe-a56a-5b96-ade0-aba6bb83e952" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278616} {:answer/id #uuid "2c4965d6-1789-5101-8609-670d36894c49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278981} {:answer/id #uuid "37793d3a-b487-5fab-a0b3-6319133e0a2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279077} {:answer/id #uuid "b8c7d88f-0dc4-56df-a7eb-7dddddb3bafa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280217} {:answer/id #uuid "f876e45a-8a6b-50b3-9bf4-f6edf08defe1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280774}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278981} :answer-field/id #uuid "1871e6ae-50f1-50ed-b4b5-c89a16ab5b1f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280875}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "048f739d-8a1c-5493-b18b-4a60653b31c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-162974" :question/problem "The lamina $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le 1\\}$ has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{15{x}^{2}}{y}.$ Find the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is represented as a type I plane region and $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{15{x}^{2}}{y}.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\cdot \\frac{15{x}^{2}}{y}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}15{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}15{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}15{x}^{2}[{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}15{x}^{2}\\cdot [y]_{y={x}^{2}}^{y=1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}15{x}^{2}\\cdot (1-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}15{x}^{2}-15{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[5{x}^{3}-3{x}^{5}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "46a434c2-8336-52c4-8ad6-467a95efe7dd" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553659}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553630 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198629 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00b03285-dd28-53bf-99ba-9f30ee298c69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278590} {:answer/id #uuid "10ce3af1-8a51-5f04-b592-aec5e5e1dfe2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278745} {:answer/id #uuid "3539077f-9040-5793-965e-5325ff444cc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279054} {:answer/id #uuid "94364912-1e0e-55a7-9d73-d9718bcfb22a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279910} {:answer/id #uuid "9b49a7ff-e06c-5346-a4c3-946264967867" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279967}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278745} :answer-field/id #uuid "71b68058-c1ae-5f51-b1c2-303e3f7cbea6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281034}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "1f4e361d-2d38-571b-8fc9-56865896c6d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-162919" :question/problem "The lamina $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le x,\\,0\\le x\\le 1\\}$ has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=3xy.$ Find the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is represented as a type I plane region and $\\lambda (x,y)=3xy.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\cdot 3xy\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}3x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}3x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot {[{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{5}{x}^{5}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "6fc4288c-ff90-587f-aa62-d32d04b0ee96" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553617}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553642 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281613 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03f5fb45-2fae-517d-b34c-c987569bdec5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278622} {:answer/id #uuid "4526b476-fcd9-5d37-a7e3-e30a4fe882ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279208} {:answer/id #uuid "52dfc9d3-54d9-5dc1-a00c-2582e20de483" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279345} {:answer/id #uuid "6fb03689-d055-5100-8394-403fc499e7d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279606} {:answer/id #uuid "942cb1e4-d459-5e88-9e20-4919448700c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279909}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279345} :answer-field/id #uuid "13279313-89f2-561e-b944-a8d52266ad9c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280864}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "13f35429-2bb3-5bdd-9f21-f76be76ab433" :question/math-academy-id "q-163152" :question/problem "The lamina $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,{y}^{2}\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\le y\\le 1\\}$ has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{1}{x}.$ Find the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is represented as a type II plane region and $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{1}{x}.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}1\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}[x]_{x={y}^{2}}^{x=1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}1-{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[y-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{y=1/2}^{y=1} \\\\  & =(1-\\frac{1}{3})-(\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{24}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{24}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "853b2b1b-be01-5e07-8544-e2b216c06e5d"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553659 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553507 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57c13dfc-1ac7-5356-938c-6c2321bc1f4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553057} {:answer/id #uuid "6fc4d700-b68c-5883-8732-9a880579eb80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553096} {:answer/id #uuid "998b0089-057f-547f-a803-33516e8d42f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553179} {:answer/id #uuid "b3c1059f-3768-5550-b92c-3b1eac23c433" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553230} {:answer/id #uuid "eaf263e5-3844-5480-8ed4-14e1d316bb2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553334}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553230} :answer-field/id #uuid "43dbda7b-1743-5761-a7b9-ff0017ff6e6e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553404}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "27367b15-5da8-51eb-9ba6-49205792b06d" :question/math-academy-id "q-162976" :question/problem "The lamina $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\}$ has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=3y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Find the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is represented as a type I plane region and $\\lambda (x,y)=3y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\cdot 3y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}3{y}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}3{y}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x[{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot {[{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{sin}^{3}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{sin}^{4}⁡x}{4}]}_{x=0}^{x=\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "a6b25d9f-7e8c-5306-983a-abf0ddccf880" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553599}}] :activity/title "Moments and Centers of Mass of Plane Laminas" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552862}]}
